{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"review\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Semantic review of the corrected artifact for C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector. The earlier artifact's accept-round observation was shown to watch the wrong round; this version drives every queued round explicitly and re-reads InstanceSpace after each delivery, and the trusted run reproduced the corrected events. The item assesses the requirement against the encoded predicates, the entry and caller duties, the oracle, identity, legal history, observation path and completion, and the contrary evidence.\\\",\n \\\"artifact_id\\\":\\\"8c65f177581c4812a6116f4a37b2b38f\\\",\n \\\"review_items\\\":[{\n  \\\"aspect\\\":\\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n  \\\"status\\\":\\\"no_issue_found\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\"],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"恢复提交与已提交命令不一致\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"在被驱动的完整恢复路径上，已提交副本报告 COMMITTED(PUT) 时恢复者仍以 NOOP 重启阶段一并完成接受轮（accept_oks 0→1），最终自己提交 COMMITTED(NOOP)：vectors_match=false，即同一实例出现两个不同的已提交命令向量。该观察覆盖本轮驱动的全部轮次与最终记录，超出该路径的后果（其它副本的提交传播、客户端可见性）不在本次检查范围内。\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requirement versus predicates: the obligation is that a slow-quorum reply reporting the instance COMMITTED is adopted; the first property asserts adopted_committed on the resolution event, and the second asserts vectors_match on the outcome event, which is the agreement form of the same requirement for the accept path. Both predicates are read from fields the harness prints together with the raw status, command and accept count, and the run reproduced adopted_committed false and vectors_match false with recoverer_command NONE against peer_committed_command PUT and accept_oks 1. Entry, schedule and completion: the harness drives Prepare/PrepareReply, the phase-1 restart's PreAccept/PreAcceptReply and the resulting Accept/AcceptReply in order, re-reading InstanceSpace after every delivery because startPhase1 replaces the record object, so the accept count that moves 0 to 1 and the COMMITTED status are read from the record the handlers actually wrote; the earlier mismatch (accept count read during the phase-1 reply, Accept never delivered) is fixed and the trailing diagnostic shows the Commit the recoverer broadcast. Oracle: vectors_match is the conjunction of the recoverer having committed and its command equalling the peer's, which is exactly the agreement question for one instance; the identity fields correlate the prerequisite reply and the outcome through the instance, not through the compared values. Legality: the peer's COMMITTED record is prepared rather than produced by a proposal round and the trigger is substituted, both declared in the claim scope; the rounds under test are the real handlers. Counterevidence and alternatives: the remaining reservations are that the property passes vacuously when the recoverer does not commit, that the propagation of the recoverer's Commit to other replicas is not driven, and that the alternative reading (a fresh ballot may legitimately outrank an older committed vbal) is answered for this path because the recoverer ends committed with a different command for an instance another replica already committed, which is the disagreement itself.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the outcome property is a conditional: if the recoverer never commits, vectors_match is true and the property would hold vacuously; the outcome event prints recoverer_committed so the applicability is visible\\\",\n   \\\"the peer's COMMITTED record is prepared and the recovery is entered directly, so this check fixes the resolution and accept rounds, not the history that produced the commit\\\",\n   \\\"the recoverer's Commit propagation to the other replicas and any client-visible effect are not driven\\\",\n   \\\"the first property's review for the earlier artifact remains valid; this review covers the corrected artifact and its re-execution\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review3.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review3.json 2>&1 | head -12\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
